.TH mbpy_3dtiles 1 "12 November 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbpy_3dtiles\fP \- Create an executable shellscript which will make the
standard 3D products of a survey (GLBs, OGC 3D Tiles tilesets and X3DOM pages)
with mbgrd2gltf, mbmesh and mbglb2tiles.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbpy_3dtiles\fP [\fB\-I\fP\fIsurveydir\fP] [\fB\-O\fP\fIroot\fP]
[\fB\-\-subdir\fP\fIname\fP] [\fB\-\-grid\fP\fIname\fP] [\fB\-\-datalist\fP\fIname\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-geoorigin=\fP\fIlon,lat,elev\fP] [\fB\-\-lift\fP\fImeters\fP]
[\fB\-L\fP\fImeters\fP] [\fB\-\-threads\fP\fIn\fP] [\fB\-\-no\-label\-chunks\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-x3dom\-url\fP\fIurl\fP] [\fB\-\-no\-survey\-page\fP]
[\fB\-\-mbgrd2gltf\-args=\fP\fIargs\fP] [\fB\-\-mbmesh\-args=\fP\fIargs\fP]
[\fB\-\-mbglb2tiles\-args=\fP\fIargs\fP]
.br
[\fB\-X\fP] [\fB\-V\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbpy_3dtiles\fP is a macro that writes a shellscript, \fIroot\fP.sh
(default 3dtiles.sh, in the survey directory), and with \fB\-X\fP runs it.
It is meant to be run in a survey directory that has a subdirectory for each
kind of data, by default \fBmultibeam\fP and \fBlidar\fP, each with a grid,
\fBZTopo.grd\fP, and a datalist of processed swath data, \fBdatalistp.mb\-1\fP.
A subdirectory, or a file in it, that is not there is left out. The commands,
in the order that they run, with paths relative to the survey directory:
.br
1. \fBmbgrd2gltf\fP \-\-input \fIdir\fP/ZTopo.grd \-\-html \-\-geoorigin \-\-output \fIdir\fP/ZTopo
.br
2. \fBmbmesh\fP \-\-input \fIdir\fP/datalistp.mb\-1 \-\-html \-\-threads \-\-geoorigin \-L
\-\-raw\-mesh\-glb \-\-pointcloud\-glb \-\-track\-glb \-\-label\-chunks \-\-output \fIdir\fP/mbmesh_output
.br
3. \fBmbglb2tiles\fP of \fIdir\fP/ZTopo.glb (to \fIdir\fP/ZTopo_tileset) and of
\fIdir\fP/mbmesh_output/mesh.glb, each with \-\-html \-\-x3dom\-url \-\-lift
.br
4. \fBmbmesh\fP \-\-input . \-\-html \-\-geoorigin \-\-x3dom\-url, the survey page, mbmesh_survey.html.
.PP
Every program gets the same GeoOrigin, so that the models line up, and every
tileset the same lift. Without \fB\-\-geoorigin\fP the GeoOrigin is the center
of the area of all the grids and the mean of their mean heights, read with \fBgmt grdinfo\fP; without
\fB\-\-lift\fP the lift puts the lowest point of the grids 10 m above the
ellipsoid, to a meter. The pages and their logs need a web server: from the
survey directory, \fBpython3 \-m http.server\fP.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-I\fIsurveydir\fP, \-\-input
The survey directory [the current directory].
.TP
.B \-O\fIroot\fP, \-\-output
The shellscript is \fIroot\fP.sh [3dtiles].
.TP
.B \-\-subdir \fIname\fP
A subdirectory to process; can be repeated [multibeam, lidar].
.TP
.B \-\-grid \fIname\fP, \-\-datalist \fIname\fP
The names of the grid and the datalist [ZTopo.grd, datalistp.mb\-1].
.TP
.B \-\-geoorigin=\fIlon,lat,elev\fP
The GeoOrigin, with the height above the ellipsoid. A value that begins with a
minus has to be attached with an equals sign.
.TP
.B \-\-lift \fImeters\fP
How far the tilesets are lifted above the ellipsoid.
.TP
.B \-L\fImeters\fP, \-\-lod
The smallest feature size of \fBmbmesh\fP [0.1].
.TP
.B \-\-threads \fIn\fP, \-\-no\-label\-chunks
Chunks that \fBmbmesh\fP reconstructs at once [8]; leave the chunk outlines out of the pages.
.TP
.B \-\-x3dom\-url \fIurl\fP
The X3DOM script of the pages of \fBmbglb2tiles\fP and the survey page
[./x3dom\-full.js]; it is relative to each page.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-survey\-page
Leave out the survey page.
.TP
.B \-\-mbgrd2gltf\-args=\fIargs\fP, \-\-mbmesh\-args=\fIargs\fP, \-\-mbglb2tiles\-args=\fIargs\fP
More options for the programs, as one quoted string.
.TP
.B \-X
Run the shellscript.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the commands and how the GeoOrigin and the lift were set.

.SH AUTHOR
Mike McCann, Monterey Bay Aquarium Research Institute, with the
MB\-System macros by David W. Caress and Dale N. Chayes.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmbgrd2gltf\fP(1), \fBmbmesh\fP(1), \fBmbglb2tiles\fP(1), \fBmbpy_grdplot\fP(1)
